	"gaits/alchemist_stroke_time": "How long this class\'s strides take, times the fish\'s stride peak and fade times. Above 1: slow, heavy strokes. Below 1: fast flicks. The sweet spot moves with it.",
	"gaits/alchemist_surface_mode": "What a stride does on a surface. None: nothing; strides only push in open water.",
	"gaits/alchemist_turn_bank": "Titans only: how far the body rolls into a turn at full turn (rad).",
	"gaits/alchemist_visual": "The model\'s animation for each stride. Tail bend: the tail sweeps across and back. Flap: the side flaps beat down with the push. Fluke: the tail beats up and down. Bell pulse: the bell contracts and expands with strides (no tail beat) and leans as it swims.",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_flatten": "Bell pulse only: how wide and flat the recovery stroke spreads the bell, its rim flaring out like an umbrella. 0: it doesn\'t open past its rest shape.",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_full_speed": "Bell push only: the speed (m/s) at which a coasting bell is fully leaned. Holding the throttle or striding leans it fully whatever the speed.",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_lean_max": "Bell push only: how far the bell leans from upright toward the nose when swimming flat out (degrees). 90: level, nose-first; 0: always upright.",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_lean_rate": "Bell push only: how quickly the bell leans to where it\'s heading (1/s).",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_recovery_time": "Bell pulse only: how long the bell takes to relax open on its own after a power stroke that no recovery stroke follows (s).",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_rhythm": "Bell pulse only: how strides drive the bell. Alternate: one stride contracts it (power stroke), the next expands it (recovery stroke). Each stride: every stride contracts it and lets it re-open.",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_ripple": "Bell pulse only: how much the bell\'s margin lags its crown and ripples, so the edge bends rather than the whole bell scaling. 0: the bell moves as one.",
	"gaits/brawler_bell_squeeze": "Bell pulse only: how hard the power stroke squeezes the bell into a tall, narrow dome. 0: it doesn\'t contract.",
	"gaits/brawler_bend_lag": "Titans only: how long the beat takes to pass from each joint to the one behind it (s): the wave\'s travel down the body. Longer: a lazier, more whip-like beat. 0: the whole body bends at once.",
	"gaits/brawler_bend_segments": "Titans only: how many joints the body bends at behind its middle, so each beat travels down it as a wave (1: one even curve, as the other fish).",
	"gaits/brawler_body_surge": "Titans only: how far the whole body surges forward on a power stroke and eases back, of its length.",
	"gaits/brawler_coast_buoyancy": "Extra lift between strides (m/s², on top of the fish\'s buoyancy). Negative sinks it while it isn\'t stroking, positive floats it up.",
	"gaits/brawler_coast_drag": "The water\'s drag between strides, times the fish\'s linear drag. Above 1: it slows down when it stops stroking (a jelly). Below 1: it coasts on (a ray). 0: no drag while coasting.",
	"gaits/brawler_flipper_trim": "Titans only: how far the flippers trim against the beat and bank in turns (0: they hold still, besides the swim\'s own flutter).",
	"gaits/brawler_fluke_amplitude": "Titans only (the adult whales\' models): how much bigger each fluke beat is than the swim\'s own, so a big tail moves a lot of water. 1: as the swim sets it.",
