	"gaits/glider_fluke_amplitude": "Titans only (the adult whales\' models): how much bigger each fluke beat is than the swim\'s own, so a big tail moves a lot of water. 1: as the swim sets it.",
	"gaits/glider_fluke_power_ratio": "Titans only: how many times slower the up-stroke (recovery) is than the down-stroke (power). 1: the same speed both ways.",
	"gaits/glider_fluke_snap": "Titans only: how quickly the flukes follow the swim\'s beat on the power stroke (1/s; the recovery follows fluke_power_ratio times slower). Lower: a softer, rounder beat that doesn\'t reach as far.",
	"gaits/glider_head_counter": "Titans only: how much the head pitches against each beat, of the body\'s bend (the nose lifts as the flukes drive down). 0: the head stays still.",
	"gaits/glider_power_stroke_speed": "Titans only: the fluke speed (rad/s) that counts as a full-strength power stroke (FishModel.power_stroke\'s strength 1; the wake, FX and sound scale with it).",
	"gaits/glider_push_axis": "What a stride pushes along. Nose: where the fish faces. Bell: along the bell, upright at rest and leaning toward the nose as it swims.",
	"gaits/glider_stroke_axis": "Which way a stride\'s side kick and the body\'s bend go. Lateral: away from the stick\'s sweep, as fish swim. Flap: up, as a wingbeat lifts. Vertical: up and down, as a whale\'s flukes beat. Radial: no kick, an even squeeze.",
	"gaits/glider_stroke_power": "How hard this class\'s strides push, times the fish\'s stride force.",
